; A top-level function can't take an operator's name. Every call of `*`
; reaches the built-in and an operator can't be passed as a value, so
; this definition could never run; it used to compile anyway. A
; parameter or local spelled `*` is fine (tests/selfhost/1005). AX2001
; at the name.
(:: * (-> Int Int Int))
(fn (* a b)
  (+ a b))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (* 6 7))
